In completeness_extraction...tex, lines 283-287, the proof says the strict PP order is a \u8220\'93well-founded DAG.\u8221\'94 A strict partial order need not be well-founded. It may contain infinite ascending or descending chains. The proof then unfolds the \u8220\'93immediate-PPI relation,\u8221\'94 i.e. the Hasse diagram, at lines 297-299. But arbitrary partial orders need not have immediate covers. Dense proper-part orders have no Hasse edges at all.}
